  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Freeze with the ball – dribble tag with rescuers",
  "description": "Every player has a ball and dribbles freely in one half of the court. One or two taggers (in bibs) dribble as well and try to tag the others with their free hand. A tagged player freezes on the spot and holds the ball with both hands above their head. A teammate frees them by dribbling one full lap around the frozen player, or by giving a high five without losing their own ball. Losing your ball or leaving the half also counts as being tagged.\n\nSwitch taggers every 45–60 seconds, or when everyone is frozen. Taggers may never stop dribbling.\n\nVariations: weak hand only, or the rescuer must dribble between the legs on the way round. More taggers make it harder, a bigger area easier.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Eyes up – you need to see both the taggers and teammates who need help."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Protect the ball with your body and arm when a tagger gets close."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Change speed and direction to get away – dribble low when it gets crowded."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Taggers: dribble under control and push players towards the sidelines."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
